Z||000000||JSocha||07-19-2001||11:38 AM||||I'm in the process of working on my brothers and his wife's website for their resort and would like some pointers on how to ensure it gets a little higher in the Search Engines Listings so as not to get SPAMMED from their lists.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.twinoaks4fun.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.twinoaks4fun.com</A> <P>For now, since I am still awaiting all the pictures, documentation and other information from them, I have put in TITLES, some general DESCRIPTIONS and a general list of KEYWORDS on all the pages (I came up with) and created to get it going and will be changing them over time as I get the information.<P>I started submitting their URL yesterday and today to the Search Engines and if somebody is willing to review the site and give me some pointers, I would surely appreciate it.<P>What are the current standards regarding META TAGS to be aware of so I don't get black listed.<P>After this (probably this winter), I am going to start working on my personal Fiero web site.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||AusFiero||07-20-2001||02:16 AM||||&lt;TITLE&gt;Put what you think most people would search for as the page title&lt;/TITLE&gt;<BR>&lt;META NAME="description" content="Your description here. Use about 300 characters"&gt;<BR>&lt;META NAME="keywords" content="lots, of, keywords, do, not, repeat, them, use, about, 100, words"&gt;<BR>&lt;META HTTP-EQUIV="Content-Type" CONTENT="text/html; CHARSET=iso-8859-1"&gt;<BR>&lt;META NAME="GENERATOR" CONTENT="Mozilla/4.61 [en] (Win98; I) [Netscape]"&gt;<BR>&lt;META NAME="robots" CONTENT="index follow"&gt;<BR>&lt;META NAME="revisit" CONTENT="15 days"&gt;<BR>&lt;META NAME="Author" CONTENT="cheat and put the business name here"&gt;<P>Basically what I seen it needs lots more keywords and description. The other bits help. Getting the robots to revisit definately helps. <P>Also create entrance pages besides the main one loaded up with keywords about say 1 particular subject and use lot of them submitted individually to the search engine. EG Fishing: use heaps of words to do with just fishing like fish, fishing, angler, angling, bait etc etc<P>More links people have to your site too also helps. That is why web developers like myself link ourselves to everything we create. <P>It is a debatable science though because the search engines are constantly changing.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
